# Testing Conventions (Vitest)

## Blackbox principle

- Tests expose bugs — do not weaken assertions to greenwash failures.
- Fix production code when behavior is wrong; change tests only for wrong expectations or intentional contract changes.
- See also: `.cursor/failing-tests-debugging.mdc`

## Organization

- Colocate tests: `Component.test.tsx` next to `Component.tsx`, or `src/lib/*.test.ts`
- Use `@testing-library/react`, `@testing-library/user-event`, `@testing-library/jest-dom`

## Pattern

```tsx
import { render, screen } from "@testing-library/react";
import userEvent from "@testing-library/user-event";
import { describe, it, expect, vi } from "vitest";

describe("MyComponent", () => {
  it("does the thing", async () => {
    const user = userEvent.setup();
    render(<MyComponent />);
    await user.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: /submit/i }));
    expect(screen.getByText("Done")).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

## API tests

- Mock `fetch` at module level; assert URL, method, headers, body.
- See `src/lib/api.test.ts` for patterns.

## Running tests

```bash
npm test -- --run                    # all
npm test -- --run src/lib/api.test.ts  # one file
```
